PaMO internal research build
===============================================

This combined binary distribution contains or derives from:

* PaMO, commit a10e34351eb7de71f41eb279e7ab9b2b101cf7a4, AGPL-3.0-only:
  https://github.com/SarahWeiii/pamo
* PDMC, commit 54406314bb9870c2c1b3c2badfde3f6d01f1e499, declared by its
  package metadata as CC BY-NC 4.0:
  https://github.com/seonghunn/pdmc
* cuMesh2SDF, commit 7789ade81bcd5fa77112d2cb5d825ed0e634e76b,
  Apache-2.0:
  https://github.com/eliphatfs/cumesh2sdf
* NVIDIA CUDA helper_math.h, Copyright (c) 2022 NVIDIA CORPORATION,
  BSD-3-Clause. Its full notice is bundled in
  licenses/NVIDIA-helper_math-BSD-3-Clause.txt.
* The Jacobi eigensolver used by the Stage 3 positive-semidefinite projection,
  attributed upstream to John Burkardt and distributed under the GNU LGPL.

This build targets Python 3.10, 3.11, and 3.12, PyTorch 2.2 or newer with
CUDA 12, warp-lang 1.16 or newer, and NVIDIA GPUs of compute capability 8.0
or newer. Each binary wheel is tagged with the PyTorch minor version and
CUDA runtime it was compiled against, for example
`pamo-0.1.0+torch2.7.cu126`. This wheel is restricted to internal,
non-commercial research use by project policy and the PDMC license.

The exact source and build metadata corresponding to this binary is included
inside the wheel at:

  share/pamo/corresponding-source/

The archive contains the local compatibility changes and all native sources
needed to rebuild the three CUDA extensions. No external publication is
required to retrieve the corresponding source.
